De La Cruz (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Texas's 15th district, redrawn before this cycle and carried by Republicans at the presidential level by seven points, has become one of the most competitive House races of the year. First-term incumbent Monica De La Cruz faces Bobby Pulido, a well-known Tejano musician. Recent surveys, including nonpartisan polls from Texas Southern University, show Pulido ahead by five to seven points, and three rating outlets call the seat a Democratic flip while most others rate it a toss-up.\n\nPulido holds a large financial edge, with about $1.4 million on hand against De La Cruz's $394,000, and outside groups have spent heavily against the incumbent while none has defended her. Prediction markets strongly favor Pulido. Still, the district's Republican lean and the advantages of incumbency keep the outcome genuinely uncertain, leaving the race in the Lean Democratic column with meaningful risk in both directions.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4454, "margin": -0.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6234, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6548, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6308, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5679, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6942, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6077, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6479, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7065, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.6601, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6541, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6766, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7121, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6611, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6572, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6619, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6805, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.6513, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-1